# 6.1.referral.yield.clinical.stone

## .what

assemble the **clinical layer** of the referral — the full detail: the venue options mapped to the
given urgency, the ranked clinician options with their access constraints and citations, and the
repeatable search method. this layer is the **engine**: it is what a clinician who wants the full
picture reads. the plain-language patient summary (6.2) sits on top of it.

## .inputs

- `2.1.venue.enumerate.yield.md` — the venue types mapped to the given urgency
- `3.1.clinician.find.yield.md` — the clinician options + citations + search method
- `4.1.access.rank.yield.md` — the walkable rank + trade-offs
- `5.1.prepare.yield.md` — the preparation sheet

## .do

- carry the **given urgency** forward verbatim (from 1.1) — do not re-judge it here
- present the **venue options** and their fit to that urgency
- present the **ranked clinician options**, each with its access constraints, trade-off, and
  bhrowser citation
- attach the **repeatable search method** so the list can be refreshed when stale
- fold in the **preparation sheet** so the clinical layer is self-contained
- carry the not-medical-advice disclaimer (this is guidance output)

## .emit

into `6.1.referral.yield.clinical.yield.md` — the full referral detail, citations intact, method
attached, disclaimer carried.

## .done when

the venue options, the ranked cited clinician options, the search method, and the prep sheet are
assembled into one clinical layer, the given urgency is carried (not re-judged), and the disclaimer
is present.
